</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3">
<p class="ltx_p" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1">Higher values of <math alttext="H_{k}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1"><semantics id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1a"><msub id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">H</mi><mi id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml">k</mi></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2">𝐻</ci><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3">𝑘</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1c">H_{k}</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.m1.1d">italic_H start_POSTSUBSCRIPT italic_k end_POSTSUBSCRIPT</annotation></semantics></math> indicate greater uncertainty in the model’s decision-making process at that position. These high-entropy positions represent promising candidates for initiating structured exploration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ltx_subsubsection" id="S4.SS1.SSS3">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.3 </span>Entropy-Sensitive Position Selection</h4>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1">
<p class="ltx_p" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2">Given the full base trajectory <math alttext="P_{\text{base}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1"><semantics id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1a"><msub id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">P</mi><mtext id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3a.cmml">base</mtext></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2">𝑃</ci><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3a.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3"><mtext id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" mathsize="70%" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3">base</mtext></ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1c">P_{\text{base}}</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1.1d">italic_P start_POSTSUBSCRIPT base end_POSTSUBSCRIPT</annotation></semantics></math>, we identify positions with maximal uncertainty by selecting the top-<math alttext="K" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1"><semantics id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1a"><mi id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml">K</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1b"><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1.1">𝐾</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1c">K</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2.1d">italic_K</annotation></semantics></math> tokens with highest entropy values. Specifically, we extract a set of entropy-sensitive positions:</p>
<table class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table" id="S4.E6">
<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math alttext="\mathcal{K}=\{k_{1},\dots,k_{K}\}" class="ltx_Math" display="block" id="S4.E6.m1.3"><semantics id="S4.E6.m1.3a"><mrow id="S4.E6.m1.3.3" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.4" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.4.cmml">𝒦</mi><mo id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.3" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.3.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.3.cmml"><mo id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.3" stretchy="false" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.3.cmml">{</mo><msub id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2.cmml">k</mi><mn id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3.cmml">1</mn></msub><mo id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.4" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.3.cmml">,</mo><mi id="S4.E6.m1.1.1" mathvariant="normal" xref="S4.E6.m1.1.1.cmml">…</mi><mo id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.5" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.3.cmml">,</mo><msub id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.2" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.2.cmml">k</mi><mi id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.3" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.3.cmml">K</mi></msub><mo id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.6" stretchy="false" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.3.cmml">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.E6.m1.3b"><apply id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3"><eq id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.3"></eq><ci id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.4.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.4">𝒦</ci><set id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2"><apply id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2">𝑘</ci><cn id="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3.cmml" type="integer" xref="S4.E6.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3">1</cn></apply><ci id="S4.E6.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.1.1">…</ci><apply id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.2">𝑘</ci><ci id="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.E6.m1.3.3.2.2.2.3">𝐾</ci></apply></set></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.E6.m1.3c">\mathcal{K}=\{k_{1},\dots,k_{K}\}</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.E6.m1.3d">caligraphic_K = { italic_k start_POSTSUBSCRIPT 1 end_POSTSUBSCRIPT , … , italic_k start_POSTSUBSCRIPT italic_K end_POSTSUBSCRIPT }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right" rowspan="1"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p class="ltx_p" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.3">which correspond to the most uncertain decision points along the reasoning path.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2">
<p class="ltx_p" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1">Top-<math alttext="K" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1"><semantics id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1.1.cmml">K</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1.1">𝐾</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1c">K</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1.m1.1d">italic_K</annotation></semantics></math> Entropy Selection</span>:
Select the indices corresponding to the <math alttext="K" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1"><semantics id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1.1.cmml">K</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1.1">𝐾</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1c">K</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m1.1d">italic_K</annotation></semantics></math> largest entropy values across the entire trajectory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2507.07017v1#bib.bib33" title="">33</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table" id="S4.E7">
<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math alttext="\mathcal{K}=\operatorname{TopK}\left(\{H_{k}\}_{k=1}^{L}\right)" class="ltx_Math" display="block" id="S4.E7.m1.2"><semantics id="S4.E7.m1.2a"><mrow id="S4.E7.m1.2.2" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.3" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.3.cmml">𝒦</mi><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.2" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.2.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.E7.m1.1.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.1.1.cmml">TopK</mi><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1a" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml">⁡</mo><mrow id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml"><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml">(</mo><msubsup id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mrow id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml"><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" stretchy="false" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">{</mo><msub id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">H</mi><mi id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">k</mi></msub><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" stretchy="false" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">}</mo></mrow><mrow id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml"><mi id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2.cmml">k</mi><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.3" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.3.cmml">1</mn></mrow><mi id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">L</mi></msubsup><mo id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.E7.m1.2b"><apply id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2"><eq id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.2"></eq><ci id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.3">𝒦</ci><apply id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1"><ci id="S4.E7.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.1.1">TopK</ci><apply id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1">superscript</csymbol><apply id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><set id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1"><apply id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2">𝐻</ci><ci id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3">𝑘</ci></apply></set><apply id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3"><eq id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1"></eq><ci id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2">𝑘</ci><cn id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.3.cmml" type="integer" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.1.3.3">1</cn></apply></apply><ci id="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.E7.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.3">𝐿</ci></apply></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.E7.m1.2c">\mathcal{K}=\operatorname{TopK}\left(\{H_{k}\}_{k=1}^{L}\right)</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S4.E7.m1.2d">caligraphic_K = roman_TopK ( { italic_H start_POSTSUBSCRIPT italic_k end_POSTSUBSCRIPT } start_POSTSUBSCRIPT italic_k = 1 end_POSTSUBSCRIPT start_POSTSUPERSCRIPT italic_L end_POSTSUPERSCRIPT )</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right" rowspan="1"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3">
<p class="ltx_p" id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.1">This strategy ensures that we focus on the most uncertain reasoning steps globally, enabling us to identify natural forks in the model’s reasoning space for structured exploration.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section class="ltx_subsubsection" id="S4.SS1.SSS4">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.4 </span>Semantic Block &amp; State Construction</h4>
<figure class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" id="S4.F2"><img alt="Refer to caption" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" height="140" id="S4.F2.g1" src="x2.png" width="407"/>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span class="ltx_text" id="S4.F2.2.1.1" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span class="ltx_text" id="S4.F2.3.2" style="font-size:90%;">Frequent tokens with the highest average entropy</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1">
<p class="ltx_p" id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1.1">As shown in Figure <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2507.07017v1#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.1.4 Semantic Block &amp; State Construction ‣ 4.1 First Return: Block Definition via Uncertainty Signals ‣ 4 FR3E: First Return, Entropy-Eliciting Explore ‣ First Return, Entropy-Eliciting Explore"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, frequent tokens with high average entropy can be identified and used as key segmentation points. This figure is adapted from prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2507.07017v1#bib.bib33" title="">33</a>]</cite>, which analyzes token-level uncertainty across model trajectories. These entropy-sensitive positions serve as natural breakpoints for segmenting the trajectory into semantically meaningful reasoning blocks. Specifically, we define the block structure based on these key points:</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p2">
