</figure>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S5.SS2.p4">
<p class="ltx_p" id="S5.SS2.p4.1">Our method generates more stable advantage estimates compared to GRPO++. As illustrated in Figure <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2507.07017v1#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.2 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ First Return, Entropy-Eliciting Explore"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the advantage values exhibit smaller fluctuations and remain tightly centered around zero throughout training. The theoretical expectation <math alttext="\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi(\cdot|s)}[A(s,a)]=0" class="ltx_math_unparsed" display="inline" id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3a"><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3"><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1"><msub id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3"><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.2">𝔼</mi><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3"><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.1">a</mi><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.2">∼</mo><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.3">π</mi><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.4"><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.4.1" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.4.2" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.4.3" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.4.4">s</mi><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.3.3.4.5" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.2">⁢</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1"><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.2" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1"><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2">A</mi><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1">⁢</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3.2"><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3.2.1" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.1.1">s</mi><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3.2.2">,</mo><mi id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.2.2">a</mi><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3.2.3" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.1.1.1.3" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.2">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3.3.3">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3b">\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi(\cdot|s)}[A(s,a)]=0</annotation><annotation encoding="application/x-llamapun" id="S5.SS2.p4.1.m1.3c">blackboard_E start_POSTSUBSCRIPT italic_a ∼ italic_π ( ⋅ | italic_s ) end_POSTSUBSCRIPT [ italic_A ( italic_s , italic_a ) ] = 0</annotation></semantics></math> is closely preserved in our approach, suggesting minimal distributional shift between the current policy and the data collection process.</p>
</div>
